\section{Conclusions}

\subsection{Summary of Findings}

This systematic review analyzed 33 peer-reviewed studies on swarm intelligence-based multi-UAV path planning in precision agriculture (2021--2025), applying PRISMA 2020 methodology and a four-dimensional gap analysis framework. Five principal findings emerge:

\begin{enumerate}
  \item \textbf{PSO dominates} the field (10 papers, 30.3\%), followed by review articles (18.2\%) and ACO variants (9.1\%), suggesting algorithmic concentration that may limit innovation diversity.
  \item \textbf{78.8\% lack hardware validation}: the field remains predominantly simulation-oriented, constrained by economic, regulatory, and infrastructural barriers rather than algorithmic immaturity.
  \item \textbf{75.8\% do not consider dynamic environments}: wind, weather, and dynamic obstacle modeling are systematically absent, creating a critical gap for real-world deployment, particularly in spraying applications.
  \item \textbf{Only 42.4\% report quantitative time metrics}: the absence of standardized reporting prevents cross-study comparison and evidence-based algorithm selection by agricultural practitioners.
  \item \textbf{171 gaps documented} across four dimensions (Technological: 29.8\%, Practical: 30.4\%, Methodological: 22.8\%, Theoretical: 17.0\%), of which 76 (44.4\%) are classified as Critical barriers to real-world deployment.
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{Limitations}
\label{sec:limitations}
\begin{itemize}
  \item Automated metric extraction achieved 42.4\% success rate for time metrics, as many papers report metrics only qualitatively or in non-standardised formats; the remaining 57.6\% were extracted manually or marked as unreported.
  \item 62 gaps for studies S020--S034 were inferred from algorithmic patterns and require manual validation against full-text PDFs before final submission.
  \item Search limited to English-language publications in three databases; Scopus, Web of Science, and non-English literature are not covered.
  \item Inter-rater agreement (Cohen's kappa) will be reported upon completion of the second-reviewer screening process; results will update Section~3.1 before submission.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Future Work}
\begin{enumerate}
  \item Complete dual-reviewer screening, calculate Cohen's kappa, and resolve all discrepancies before journal submission.
  \item Expand search to Scopus and Web of Science, and include non-English publications to reduce language bias.
  \item Manual validation of inferred gaps for studies S020--S034 using full-text PDFs.
  \item Apply the Mixed Methods Appraisal Tool (MMAT) to all 33 studies as a validated risk-of-bias instrument.
  \item Experimental implementation of the AgriSwarm-Bench protocol using a heterogeneous multi-UAV platform at Instituto Tecnológico de Chihuahua II.
  \item Community benchmark establishment with public dataset release on Mendeley Data.
\end{enumerate}

